WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.000
Two ways to process data: batch or streaming.

00:03.000 --> 00:05.500
Both read from a source, run in Dataflow and end in BigQuery.

00:05.500 --> 00:12.200
Batch: files pile up in Cloud Storage first, then one Dataflow job processes them together.

00:12.200 --> 00:14.200
BigQuery receives one result after the whole run.

00:14.200 --> 00:22.600
Streaming: events arrive through Pub/Sub and Dataflow processes each one as it arrives.

00:22.600 --> 00:24.900
BigQuery keeps updating within seconds.

00:24.900 --> 00:29.900
Batch means finite data with results after the run. Streaming means unbounded data with results in seconds.
